Recently I discovered several magic markers in a game;  Using them with 
great abandon, I first wrote up a bunch of enchant armors;  not satisfied
with that, I started writing genocide scrolls, cursing them with unholy
water, and gating in wraiths in great bunches.  However, I noticed that
my magic markers seemed to dry out awfully fast.  "What's this?" quoth I.
"Perhaps it takes more than one charge to write a scroll?"

Indeed, this is the case.  Following is a table (originally from the Wheaton
spoiler sheets) with a column added on for how many charges it takes to write
the scroll.  genocide 30... no *wonder* those pens were wearing out!

(Incidently, to figure out if a scroll will be blessed when you write it,
it uses both the enchantment on the scroll and the marker, adding the two
together.  Thus blessed + normal = blessed, blessed + cursed = normal,
cursed+normal = cursed, etc).


								Cost
  Name             Prob  Cost  To Write
------------------------------------
| amnesia         |  35 | 200 |	 8 |
| blank paper     |  28 |  60 |	 * |
| charging        |  15 | 300 |	16 |
| confuse monster |  53 | 100 |	12 |
| create monster  |  45 | 200 |	10 |
| destroy armor   |  45 | 100 |	10 |
| enchant armor   |  63 |  80 |	16 |
| enchant weapon  |  85 |  60 |	16 |
| fire            |  48 | 100 |	 8 |
| food detection  |  25 | 100 |	 8 |
| genocide        |  15 | 300 |	30 |
| gold detection  |  33 | 100 |	 8 |
| identify        | 185 |  20 |	14 |
| light           |  95 |  50 |	 8 |
| magic mapping   |  45 | 100 |	 8 |
| punishment      |  15 | 300 |	10 |
| remove curse    |  65 |  80 |	16 |
| scare monster   |  35 | 100 |	20 |
| taming          |  15 | 200 |	20 |
| teleportation   |  55 | 100 |	20 |
------------------------------------

* - can't be created with a magic marker
